   "name": "Unit 1 review",
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "Measurement compares a quantity with an agreed standard. Fundamental quantities (length, mass, time, temperature) give derived ones (area, volume, speed, density). Prefixes shorten big and small numbers. Accuracy is closeness to the true value; precision is agreement. The scientific method has six steps."
    }
   },
